</guid><pubDate>2026-09-21T15:11:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aashish Vashistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134385867,imgsize-59004.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet 'Little Einstein' Laurent Simons: 16-year-old PhD holder now researching how to slow human ageing]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134385383.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[At just 16 years old, Laurent Simons has achieved remarkable academic feats, completing a PhD in theoretical quantum physics and diving into a second doctorate in medical science and artificial intelligence. His groundbreaking research aims to unravel the mysteries of ageing and enhance human longevity. Despite his extraordinary intellect, he embraces the joys of typical teenage life in-between his studies, showcasing a well-rounded personality.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/meet-little-einstein-laurent-simons-16-year-old-phd-holder-who-is-now-researching-how-to-slow-human-ageing-and-extend-lifespan/articleshow/134385383.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/meet-little-einstein-laurent-simons-16-year-old-phd-holder-who-is-now-researching-how-to-slow-human-ageing-and-extend-lifespan/articleshow/134385383.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-21T15:01:33+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134385704,imgsize-907775.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Egyptian archaeologists uncovered rare rock-cut tombs at an ancient Nile Delta site]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134385821.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In an exciting archaeological discovery, experts in Egypt announced the unearthing of unusual rock-cut tombs at Tell el-Yahudiya, tracing back to the New Kingdom and continuing through the Late Period. Above these ancient burials, traces of a Roman encampment were uncovered, highlighting how the location remained significant across multiple historical timelines, illuminating Tell el-Yahudiya's legacy.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/egyptian-archaeologists-uncovered-rare-rock-cut-tombs-at-an-ancient-nile-delta-site-with-roman-camp-remains-found-in-the-layers-above/articleshow/134385821.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/egyptian-archaeologists-uncovered-rare-rock-cut-tombs-at-an-ancient-nile-delta-site-with-roman-camp-remains-found-in-the-layers-above/articleshow/134385821.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-21T17:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134385997,imgsize-129510.cms"/></item></channel></rss>